{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.GSFiltrationUnitObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GSFiltrationUnitObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Submodule.Lattice","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CentreGradingObstruction"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.antidiagonal_pairing_excluded_at_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.antidiagonal_pairing_excluded_at_four","kind":"theorem","line":403,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSFiltrationUnitObstruction.lean#L403-L417","doc":"**The anti-diagonal strata pairing is unavailable at `n = 4`.**\n\nInstantiating §6 against `gbDepth_ne_on_H4`. This refutes\n`rem:quantum-dilogarithm-stratified-partial-argument` Step 1 **without using the word filtration\nat all** — so, unlike the six sites' shared defect, it is not repaired by\nsupplying the missing word/partition bridge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.antidiagonal_pairing_forces_constant_grading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.antidiagonal_pairing_forces_constant_grading","kind":"theorem","line":375,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSFiltrationUnitObstruction.lean#L375-L401","doc":"**An anti-diagonal pairing law on idempotent strata forces the grading to\nbe constant.**\n\n`hanti` is the block's own displayed hypothesis, restricted to the spanning\nidempotents (so it is *weaker* than what the block asserts, which makes the\nrefutation stronger). `hidem` and `hφ` are the two structural inputs.\n\nThe argument is three lines: were some `l` to have `2 · deg l ≠ N`, `hanti`\nwould give `φ(e_l · e_l) = 0`, i.e. `φ(e_l) = 0` by idempotency, contradicting\n`hφ`. So every degree is `N / 2`, hence all equal.\n\n`φ` is taken as a bare function, not a linear map: linearity is never used, and\nthe weaker hypothesis makes the theorem stronger. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.monomial_hypotheses_satisfiable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.monomial_hypotheses_satisfiable","kind":"theorem","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSFiltrationUnitObstruction.lean#L311-L330","doc":"**Every §3 hypothesis, discharged simultaneously.** So\n`monomial_filtration_forces_constant_grading` is a genuine implication: its\nantecedent has a model, and the model's grading is constant, as the theorem\npredicts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.monomial_filtration_excluded_at_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.monomial_filtration_excluded_at_four","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSFiltrationUnitObstruction.lean#L253-L286","doc":"**No filtration monomial in the Gröbner–Shirshov normal-form basis induces\nthe `gbDepth` grading on `Z(H₄(q))`.**\n\nThis is the answer to the question bean `qou-09e0` was opened on. The front was\n*\"find a filtration putting a second central element in `F_1`\"*; the obstruction\nis that a monomial filtration admitting **any** `e_λ` must admit `T_e = 1` too,\nbecause `τ(e_λ) ≠ 0` — and then it must admit every other `e_μ` as well, so it\ncannot separate the strata at all. There is no `F_1` with two central elements\nand not all of them.\n\n**Not vacuous.** Every hypothesis is separately satisfiable — the Wedderburn-\nblock filtration realises all of them but `hmono`, and the trivial filtration\n`F k = ⊤` realises all of them (including `hmono`) at `n ≤ 3`, where `deg`\ngenuinely is constant. What is impossible is the conjunction *with* a\nnon-constant grading, which is what `gbDepth_ne_on_H4` supplies. Each of `hmono`,\n`hτ`, `hu` and `hbot` is used in the proof term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.unit_degree_zero_filtration_excluded_at_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.unit_degree_zero_filtration_excluded_at_four","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSFiltrationUnitObstruction.lean#L234-L251","doc":"**No filtration placing the unit in degree `0` induces the `gbDepth` grading\non `Z(H₄(q))`.**\n\n`a` and `b` are the index-set elements carrying the two partitions of `4` whose\ndepths differ; everything else is the §2 hypothesis set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.monomial_filtration_forces_constant_grading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.monomial_filtration_forces_constant_grading","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSFiltrationUnitObstruction.lean#L197-L217","doc":"**A filtration monomial in the Gröbner–Shirshov normal-form basis forces the\npartition grading to be constant.**\n\nAntisymmetry of `strata_below_of_monomial` applied at both indices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.strata_below_of_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.strata_below_of_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSFiltrationUnitObstruction.lean#L161-L195","doc":"**Every stratum lies at or below `deg l₀`, for each `l₀`** — the engine of\nthe monomial case.\n\nThe idempotent `e l₀` lives in its own stratum, hence in `F (deg l₀ - c)`. It\nhas nonzero trace, so monomiality drags the **unit** into that same piece; and\n§1 then puts the whole grading below `deg l₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.unit_in_degree_zero_forces_constant_grading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.unit_in_degree_zero_forces_constant_grading","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSFiltrationUnitObstruction.lean#L118-L148","doc":"**If the unit is in filtration degree `0`, the partition grading is\nconstant.**\n\nImmediate from §1: `1 ∈ Z ⊓ F 0 = V c` puts every stratum at or below `c`,\nwhile `hbot` (which is `Z ⊓ F_{-1} = 0`, i.e. the filtration starts at `0`)\nputs every stratum at or above `c`.\n\nThis covers, in one stroke, **every** reading of `J^•` in which the empty word\nhas depth `0` — which is all three of them, and is what \"definable from the\nrewriting data\" means in practice. It needs no monomiality at all, so it also\nexcludes non-monomial candidates such as the Jucys–Murphy content filtration\n`Z_{≤d} = span of symmetric functions in the `L_i` of degree ≤ d`, whose degree-\n`0` piece is `R·1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.all_strata_below_of_unit_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.all_strata_below_of_unit_mem","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSFiltrationUnitObstruction.lean#L96-L114","doc":"**If the unit lies in stratum `j`, then every stratum is at or below `j`.**\n\n`1 = Σ_λ e_λ` has *every* coordinate equal to `1`, so it cannot be missing any\nidempotent — and `V j` is precisely the span of those with `deg ≤ j`. This is\nthe half that pushes the unit to the top of the filtration.\n\nNote it uses `Nontrivial R` essentially: over the zero ring `1 = 0` and the\nstatement is false. ","signatureChunk":0}]}